Package: SurvX
Type: Package
Title: Survival and Competing Risks Analysis with Direct Parametric Models for the Cumulative Incidence Function
Version: 0.9.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Habib", "Ezzatabadipour", email = "habibezati@outlook.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Robert", "Gray", role = "cph",
           comment = "variance computation of the K-sample test, ported from the Fortran routine crstm of package cmprsk"))
Description: A dependency-free C++ core with an S7 interface for survival and competing
    risks analysis: Kaplan-Meier and Aalen-Johansen estimators, log-rank and Gray tests, Cox,
    cause-specific Cox and Fine-Gray regression, and the direct parametric models for the
    cumulative incidence function of Jeong and Fine (2006) <doi:10.1111/j.1467-9876.2006.00532.x>
    and Jeong and Fine (2007) <doi:10.1093/biostatistics/kxj040> with Gompertz, Weibull, mixture,
    modified logistic and spline baselines and proportional hazards, proportional odds and
    generalized odds rate links. Parametric survival regression (exponential, Weibull, Gompertz,
    log-normal, log-logistic; proportional hazards or accelerated failure time; delayed entry),
    parametric cause-specific hazards with cumulative incidence by numerical integration, and the
    Nelson-Aalen and kernel-smoothed hazard. Prediction performance (Brier score, index of prediction
    accuracy, time-dependent AUC, calibration) and cross-validated model comparison are included.
